    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d124">

                <pb facs="0163" n="149" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg149"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.333D3/1651a: Circular telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Certain Diplomatic
                        Representatives in the American Republics </hi><anchor n="18"
                        xml:id="d124-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-02">June 2, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>At meeting of the Inter-American Coffee Board, May 31, the Colombian Government
                    notified the Board that Colombia is agreeable to continuation of the
                    Inter-American Coffee Agreement for one year from October 1, 1944. Since this
                    completes acceptances by participating countries, Agreement will be continued in
                    accordance with Article XXIV thereof.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d124-f1" n="18" type="source" xml:id="d124-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to Colombia, Brazil, Venezuela, El Salvador, Mexico, Guatemala, Nicaragua,
                    Costa Rica, Honduras, Cuba, Dominican Republic, Haiti, Ecuador, and Peru.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
